    "lower6-maths-ap-gp-q3",
    "lower6-maths-ap-gp-q4",
    "lower6-maths-ap-gp-q5"
   ],
   "reviewNotes": [
    "Sigma notation and recurrence relations $u_{n+1}=f(u_n)$ are not covered here.",
    "Syllabus references, scope and level of difficulty are to be checked against the official text; all facts, formulas and worked examples to be verified by a teacher before release."
   ],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Arithmetic progression (AP)",
     "md": "First term $a$, common difference $d$: $u_n=a+(n-1)d$ and $S_n=\\frac{n}{2}\\big(2a+(n-1)d\\big)=\\frac{n}{2}(a+l)$ where $l$ is the last term."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Geometric progression (GP)",
     "md": "First term $a$, common ratio $r$: $u_n=ar^{n-1}$ and $S_n=\\frac{a(1-r^n)}{1-r}$ ($r\\neq1$). If $|r|<1$ the series converges to $S_\\infty=\\frac{a}{1-r}$."
    },
    {
     "type": "illustration",
     "figure": {
      "kind": "bars",
      "w": 400,
      "h": 240,
      "bars": [
       {
        "label": "Y1",
        "value": 800,
        "color": "blue"
       },
       {
        "label": "Y2",
        "value": 880,
        "color": "blue"
       },
       {
        "label": "Y3",
        "value": 968,
        "color": "blue"
       },
       {
        "label": "Y4",
        "value": 1065,
        "color": "blue"
       },
       {
        "label": "Y5",
        "value": 1171,
        "color": "blue"
       },
       {
        "label": "Y6",
        "value": 1288,
        "color": "blue"
       }
      ],
      "unit": "kg"
     },
     "caption": "Yearly cocoa harvest growing by 10% per year: a geometric progression.",
     "alt": "Six bars of increasing height from 800 kg to about 1288 kg."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Method",
     "md": "Write what you know as equations in $a$ and $d$ (or $a$ and $r$), solve them, then apply the sum formula. For a GP, find $r$ by dividing a term by the previous one. Always check $|r|<1$ before using $S_\\infty$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- The nth term uses $(n-1)$, not $n$.\n- $S_\\infty$ does NOT exist if $|r|\\geq1$.\n- Do not confuse $u_n$ (one term) with $S_n$ (sum of $n$ terms)."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "An AP has 5th term 17 and 12th term 52. Find $a$, $d$ and $S_{20}$.",
     "steps": [
      "$u_{12}-u_5=7d=35$, so $d=5$.",
      "$a+4d=17$ gives $a=-3$.",
      "$S_{20}=10\\big(2(-3)+19\\times5\\big)=10\\times89$."
     ],
     "answer": "$a=-3$, $d=5$, $S_{20}=890$"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "A GP begins $8,\\,12,\\,18,s'$ Find $u_6$. Then find $S_\\infty$ of $20+10+5+\\cdots$",
     "steps": [
      "$r=\\frac{12}{8}=1.5$ and $u_6=8\\times1.5^5=60.75$.",
      "For $20+10+5+\\cdots$: $a=20$, $r=\\frac{1}{2}$, so $S_\\infty=\\frac{20}{1-0.5}$."
     ],
     "answer": "$u_6=60.75$; $S_\\infty=40$"
    }
   ],
   "chapter": "lower6-maths-sequences"
